+### Bolt
+
+Bolt posts `{ "event_id", "event_type", "amount", "currency", "charge_id" }`
+with the amount as a decimal string such as `"125.00"`. `event_type` is one of
+`charge.succeeded`, `charge.failed` or `charge.refunded`, which we map to
+`payment.succeeded`, `payment.failed` and `refund.created`; `charge_id`
+becomes the payment's external id. Each request carries
+`x-bolt-signature: <base64>`, the HMAC-SHA256 of the raw request body keyed
+with `BOLT_WEBHOOK_SECRET`. Bolt does not sign a timestamp, so there is no
+tolerance window; a redelivered event is caught by the same
+`(provider, external_id)` uniqueness as Acme's.
+
 ## API
 
